# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# apps/studio/.env.example — copy to apps/studio/.env.local (gitignored).
#
# STANDALONE. The Studio inherits NOTHING from the repo root: Vite only reads
# env files in this directory, and only keys prefixed SANITY_STUDIO_ reach the
# bundle. So every value the Studio needs is repeated here — these are not
# redundant copies of root, they are the only ones it can see.
#
# Precedence for `sanity dev` (development mode):
#     shell env  >  .env.development.local  >  .env.local  >  .env
# Precedence for `sanity build` / `sanity deploy` (PRODUCTION mode):
#     shell env  >  .env.production  >  .env.local  >  .env
#
# Note the second row: `.env.production` OUTRANKS `.env.local`. This file
# therefore steers LOCAL `sanity dev` ONLY. A DEPLOYED Studio is steered by
# `pnpm sanity:deploy:staging|prod`, which export their whole target from
# TARGETS in scripts/sanity/studio-targets.mjs — editing the preview URLs here
# does not change pakfactory-staging.sanity.studio.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Must match the project + dataset you seeded (`pnpm seed` / `pnpm seed:blog-dev`).
# Rewritten in place by `pnpm studio:local|staging|prod`.
# When introducing a new var, also add it to `turbo.json` env lists if apps consume it at build time.

SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=""
SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET="development"

# ── Presentation preview bases (local `sanity dev` only) ─────────────────────
# A TRAILING SLASH is required on all three: Presentation resolves the relative
# draft-mode `enable` path against the base, and without it the last path
# segment is replaced instead of appended (PROD-2223).
# Whatever you set must also appear in that workspace's `allowOrigins` in
# sanity.config.ts, or Presentation refuses to frame it.
#
#   BLOG  the blog app. Local runs at the origin root (no /blog basePath).
#   WWW   the case-studies surface. Carries the /case-studies/ path, because the
#         draft-mode enable route lives under it (PROD-2223).
#   SITE  the whole-site target for the seven content workspaces (PROD-2494).
SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_URL_BLOG="http://localhost:3003/"
SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_URL_WWW="http://localhost:3000/case-studies/"
SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_URL_SITE="http://localhost:3000/"

# Non-interactive deploy auth is SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN — that exact name is what the
# Sanity CLI looks for. (`SANITY_API_DEPLOY_TOKEN` is NOT read by anything.)
# Leave unset to authenticate as your logged-in CLI session instead.
# SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN=""
